2026-10-10T04:07:20.4939267Z == S1  the quantum dictionary
2026-10-10T04:07:20.5385345Z PASS D1  [identity] pauliW (cnot w) = CNOT pauliW(w) CNOT^dagger for a symbolic table w (cnot is conjugation by CNOT)
2026-10-10T04:07:20.5402904Z PASS D2  [identity] cnot . cnot = id on a symbolic table
2026-10-10T04:07:20.5947527Z PASS D3  [identity] ipW E X = tr(opW(E) pauliW(X)) for symbolic E, X (the Euclidean pairing is the trace pairing)
2026-10-10T04:07:20.6359875Z PASS D4  [identity] pairVal a b w = tr((opV a (x) opV b) pauliW(w)) for symbolic a, b, w
2026-10-10T04:07:20.6595206Z PASS D5  [identity] pauliW (prodState x y) = rho(x) (x) rho(y), rho(x) = (I + x.s)/2, for symbolic x, y
2026-10-10T04:07:20.6625096Z PASS D6  [identity] opV a is Hermitian with trace 2 a0 and determinant a0^2 - |a|^2 (opV a >= 0 iff a in L)
2026-10-10T04:07:21.2590515Z PASS D7  [identity] for a symbolic quaternion q, U = q0 I - i q.s gives U s_k U^dagger = sum_i M_ik s_i with M^T M = |q|^4 I, det M = |q|^6, and pauliW(diag(|q|^2, M) w) = (U (x) I) pauliW(w) (U (x) I)^dagger (and on the second token)
2026-10-10T04:07:21.2594081Z NOTE [written] D7.W  -- at |q| = 1, M is a rotation and actC M = Ad(U (x) I), actT M = Ad(I (x) U); every U in SU(2) is of this form, and every rotation is M for some unit quaternion (the standard double cover SU(2) -> SO(3)). So actC R and actT R for rotations R are exactly the conjugations by local unitaries, and Q3, int Q3 are invariant under them.
2026-10-10T04:07:21.2597684Z NOTE [written] D.W  -- by D3 and the self-duality of the positive semidefinite cone under the trace pairing, dualW Q3 = {E : opW E >= 0}; by D4 and D6, Q3 lies in maxCone (opV a (x) opV b >= 0 for a, b in L); by D5 and D6, every prodState x y with x, y in eball 3 lies in Q3; by D1, cnot maps Q3 onto Q3 and int Q3 onto int Q3.
2026-10-10T04:07:21.2599698Z 
2026-10-10T04:07:21.2600059Z == S2  an explicit carrier for KT4Core
2026-10-10T04:07:21.2604020Z NOTE [written] S2.def  -- V = R^{17x17} x R^{17x17}. For x in R^16 let xh = (1, x) and X the table X_ab = x_{4a+b}; for an affine e(x) = e0 + E.x let eh = (e0, E) and Et the table Et_ab = E_{4a+b} + e0 [a = b = 0]. stA x y = (xh yh^T, 0), stB x y = (0, xh yh^T); effA e f (P, Q) = eh^T P fh + sum_abcd Et_ab Ft_cd Q[1 + (4a+c), 1 + (4b+d)]; effB e f (P, Q) = eh^T Q fh + sum_abcd Et_ac Ft_bd P[1 + (4a+b), 1 + (4c+d)]. Both are linear in (P, Q) and bilinear in (e, f). The index map (a, b) -> 4a + b stands for the bijection flatW and tabCoord use; the identities below hold for any fixed bijection used consistently.
2026-10-10T04:07:21.3999297Z PASS H1  [identity] effA e f (stA x y) = e(x) f(y) for symbolic affine e, f and symbolic x, y in R^16
2026-10-10T04:07:21.4717466Z PASS H2  [identity] effB e f (stB x y) = e(x) f(y) for symbolic affine e, f and symbolic x, y in R^16
2026-10-10T04:07:25.5992831Z PASS H3  [identity] effA and effB are linear in each effect argument, on a symbolic element of V
2026-10-10T04:07:26.9067461Z PASS H4  [identity] tokA: effA (tabCoord a b) (tabCoord c d) (stA x y) = effB (tabCoord a c) (tabCoord b d) (stA x y), all 256 index quadruples, symbolic x, y -- 256/256
2026-10-10T04:07:28.1920056Z PASS H5  [identity] tokB: the same with stB x y, all 256 index quadruples, symbolic x, y -- 256/256
2026-10-10T04:07:28.4536808Z PASS H6  [identity] effB e f (stA x y) = fourVal X Y Et Ft (the cross value of grouping 02|13 effects on 01|23 states)
2026-10-10T04:07:28.6870154Z PASS H7  [identity] effA e f (stB x y) = sum Et_ab Ft_cd X_ac Y_bd (the cross value of 01|23 effects on 02|13 states)
2026-10-10T04:07:29.2467782Z PASS H8  [identity] fourVal X Y E F = ipW X (tabMul (tabMul E Y) (tabT F)) = ipW E (X F Y^T) for symbolic tables (famI is the positivity of this value)
2026-10-10T04:07:29.4653006Z PASS H9  [identity] sum e_ab f_cd L_ac L'_bd = ipW e (tabMul (tabMul L f) (tabT L')) for symbolic tables (the famII form)
2026-10-10T04:07:29.4687393Z PASS H10  [identity] e(flat X) = ipW Et X when X_00 = 1, symbolic e and X (an effect on a pair body is its table on the slice)
2026-10-10T04:07:29.4692360Z NOTE [written] H.W  -- let K02, K13 lie in maxCone and be closed under nonnegative scaling. If e is an effect on pairBody K02 then Et lies in dualW K02: a nonzero w in K02 has w_00 > 0 (in maxCone, w_00 >= 0, and w_00 = 0 forces w = 0, from a^T w b at a = (1, u), b = (1, v)), and ipW Et w = w_00 e(flat(w / w_00)) >= 0 by H10. Then posBA is famI at (X, Y, Et, Ft) by H6 and H8, and posAB is famII by H7 and H9. Together with H1, H2, H4, H5 and H3: FCC, the maxCone bound and nonnegative scaling of the four cones give KT4Core on this V. Conversely Lemma B1 (fourCopyCoherent_of_kt4Core, kernel-checked in the design module FourCopyBridge) gives FCC from KT4Core and the same two clauses. Under hadm the hypothesis H is therefore equivalent to FCC, by separately named arguments in each direction.
2026-10-10T04:07:29.4697427Z 
2026-10-10T04:07:29.4697677Z == S3  FCC for uniform Q3 and for uniform maxCone
2026-10-10T04:07:29.4698368Z PASS F0  [identity] Pi is a permutation matrix (Pi Pi^T = I)
2026-10-10T04:07:29.4705535Z PASS F1  [enumerate] tr(s_m s_n) = 2 delta_mn for the four Pauli matrices -- 16 pairs
2026-10-10T04:07:37.4832751Z PASS F2  [identity] fourVal X Y E F = tr( Pi (opW E (x) opW F) Pi^T (pauliW X (x) pauliW Y) ), symbolic X, Y, E, F (E on tokens 0, 2; F on 1, 3; X on 0, 1; Y on 2, 3)
2026-10-10T04:07:38.0625912Z PASS F3  [identity] sum e_ab f_cd L_ac L'_bd = tr( (opW e (x) opW f) Pi (pauliW L (x) pauliW L') Pi^T ), symbolic (the famII form, L on tokens 0, 2 and L' on 1, 3)
2026-10-10T04:07:38.0751543Z PASS F2v  [sample] sample inputs: pauliW of each of phiW, T_psi, diag(1,-1,-1,-1), E00 and opW of each of phiW/4, diag(1,-1,-1,-1)/4, E00, T_psi/4 are positive semidefinite (exact eigenvalues)
2026-10-10T04:07:38.6756691Z PASS F2s  [sample] sample: fourVal X Y E F >= 0 at the 256 quadruples of these entangled and product states of Q3 and entangled and product effects of dualW Q3 -- minimum 0
2026-10-10T04:07:38.6761161Z NOTE [written] F.Q3  -- FCC for uniform Q3: for X, Y in Q3 and E, F in dualW Q3, opW E, opW F, pauliW X, pauliW Y are positive semidefinite (S1); the Kronecker product of positive semidefinite matrices is positive semidefinite (Mathlib Matrix.PosSemidef.kronecker), conjugation by the permutation Pi preserves this, and the trace of a product of two positive semidefinite matrices is nonnegative. By F2 famI holds, by F3 famII holds.
2026-10-10T04:07:38.8280783Z PASS F4  [identity] pairVal a b (X F Y^T) = ipW F ((X^T a)(Y^T b)^T), symbolic
2026-10-10T04:07:38.8371279Z PASS F5  [identity] pairVal a b (u v^T) = (a.u)(b.v), symbolic
2026-10-10T04:07:38.8418057Z PASS F6  [identity] Lagrange: |a|^2 |u|^2 - (a.u)^2 = sum_{i<j} (a_i u_j - a_j u_i)^2 in R^3 (Cauchy-Schwarz)
2026-10-10T04:07:38.8420946Z NOTE [written] F.max  -- FCC for uniform maxCone: the homogeneous coefficient vector of an effect on eball 3 lies in L, and every vector of L is a positive multiple of one, so maxCone = {w : a^T w b >= 0 for a, b in L}. L is self-dual for the Euclidean pairing (F6). For X, Y in maxCone and a, b in L: u = X^T a and v = Y^T b lie in L, so u v^T lies in maxCone (F5) and a^T (X F Y^T) b = ipW F (u v^T) >= 0 for F in dualW maxCone (F4). So X F Y^T lies in maxCone, and fourVal X Y E F = ipW E (X F Y^T) >= 0 for E in dualW maxCone (H8): famI. famII is the same argument for (L, F, L') (H9).
2026-10-10T04:07:38.8440515Z PASS F7  [witness] opW(phiW/4) is a rank-one projector, so phiW/4 lies in dualW Q3
2026-10-10T04:07:38.8505483Z PASS F8  [witness] ipW F (actT reflY w) = ipW (actT reflY F) w (symbolic), and opW(actT reflY F) is a rank-one projector for F = diag(1, -1, 1, -1)/4, so F lies in dualW twin
2026-10-10T04:07:38.8521164Z PASS F9  [witness] pauliW phiW is a rank-one projector (phiW in Q3)
2026-10-10T04:07:38.8546947Z PASS F10  [countercontrol] famI fails for the cones (Q3, Q3, Q3, twin): fourVal phiW phiW (phiW/4) F = -1/8 -- value -1/8
